---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const authors = await getCollection('authors');

const CHECKS = [
  { n: 1, label: 'Primary source found and linked', body: 'Every article links to an official document, press release, or outlet report — not a third-hand retelling.' },
  { n: 2, label: 'On-chain data confirms the claim', body: "Where it applies, figures are checked directly against the blockchain or a public API, not taken on the source's word." },
  { n: 3, label: 'An independent second outlet reports the same thing', body: 'One source is a reason for caution. We look for independent confirmation before marking a story "Confirmed."' },
  { n: 4, label: "The other party's official statement is on record", body: "If a story involves a company or protocol, we try to record their official position, not just the affected or attacking side's version." },
  { n: 5, label: 'Numbers checked by the editors', body: 'Amounts, percentages, and dates are recomputed independently by the editorial team — a discrepancy between sources is itself a reason to write about it, not something we paper over.' },
  { n: 6, label: 'Signed off by the editor on duty', body: 'A final pass before publication: the logic of the piece, whether the numbers match their sources, whether related links are correct.' },
];

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'AboutPage',
    name: 'About — Finality',
    about: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Finality' },
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  locale="en"
  title="About Finality: How We Verify Crypto News"
  description="How Finality verifies news, who writes it, and what we do when the facts don't line up."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="wrap page">
    <nav class="crumbs"><a href="/en/">Finality</a> / About</nav>
    <h1 class="title">About</h1>
    <p class="intro">
      Finality is the pilot title of a planned five-outlet crypto and fintech media network, built
      around one idea: every number in a news story should have a checkable source. Below is how
      that actually works, not just the slogan version.
    </p>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Verification methodology</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Every article runs through a verification log — up to six checks, visible to the reader
        right on the story page, each with the date it was cleared. Not all six apply to every
        story: "on-chain data," for instance, is meaningless for a story about a bill in Congress.
      </p>
      <ol class="checks">
        {CHECKS.map((c) => (
          <li>
            <span class="check-num data">{c.n}</span>
            <div>
              <p class="check-label">{c.label}</p>
              <p class="check-body">{c.body}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <p class="note">
        A "Developing" status means some checks haven't cleared yet — usually because an
        independent second outlet hasn't confirmed the details, or a party hasn't responded to a
        request for comment. It isn't a draft: whatever's already published was already verified
        as of the moment it went live.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>The team</h2>
      <div class="team">
        {authors.map((author) => (
          <a href={`/en/author/${author.id}/`} class="team-card">
            <span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">{author.data.initials}</span>
            <div>
              <p class="name">{author.data.name}</p>
              <p class="role kicker">{author.data.role_en ?? author.data.role}</p>
              <p class="bio">{author.data.bio_en ?? author.data.bio}</p>
            </div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>What's honest to say about being a pilot</h2>
      <p>
        Finality is the first site of a planned network, and at this stage part of the editorial
        scaffolding is labeled as such rather than presented as more than it is. The three authors
        above are real editorial beats with real topic specialization, but without published
        photos or links to personal social accounts — adding a placeholder link would fabricate a
        digital identity that doesn't exist. Once a real editor is attached to each beat, the
        profile will be updated.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sponsored placements (for example, on the "Projects" page) are always marked with a
        separate label and physically kept apart from the editorial rankings — a paid placement
        cannot affect which row ranks higher in a table.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>If we got something wrong</h2>
      <p>
        A factual discrepancy is something that should be corrected in public, not quietly rewritten
        away. Grounds for a correction are a new primary source or a clarification of one already
        cited — not a disagreement with interpretation. At the pilot stage, Finality doesn't yet
        have a dedicated public channel for this kind of report — better to say that plainly than
        to point at contacts that don't exist yet.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-block: 24px 48px;
    max-width: 760px;
  }
  .crumbs {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--graphite);
  }
  .crumbs a {
    color: var(--graphite);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .title {
    font-size: var(--step-h1);
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .intro {
    max-width: 68ch;
    color: var(--graphite);
    margin: 16px 0 40px;
  }
  .block {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .block h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-h3);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .lead {
    color: var(--graphite);
    max-width: 62ch;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }
  .checks {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-top: 16px;
  }
  .checks li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 24px 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .check-num {
    color: var(--graphite);
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .check-label {
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .check-body {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--graphite);
    font-size: 14px;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .note {
    color: var(--graphite);
    font-size: 13px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-top: 16px;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .team {
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .team-card {
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--ink);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: 16px;
  }
  .team-card:hover {
    background: var(--paper);
  }
  .avatar {
    width: 48px;
    height: 48px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--ledger);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: var(--font-data);
    font-size: 16px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .name {
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .role {
    margin: 2px 0 6px;
  }
  .bio {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--graphite);
    font-size: 13px;
    max-width: 52ch;
  }
</style>
